eq;\\\\n\\\" +\\n\",\n      \"new\": \"            string.Join(\\\", \\\", Enumerable.Range(4, 96)) + \\\" FROM seq ORDER BY id OPTION (MAXDOP 1);\\\\n\\\" +\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"sqlserver\/manual-count-100m\/lab.rb\",\n      \"old\": \"    @cleanup_deadline = now + 120\\n\",\n      \"new\": \"    @cleanup_deadline = now + 240\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"sqlserver\/manual-count-100m\/lab.rb\",\n      \"old\": \"            docker('stop', '--time', '20', id, cleanup: true, seconds: 25)\\n\",\n      \"new\": \"            stop_seconds = name == \\\"#{PREFIX}-client\\\" ? 20 : 60\\n            docker('stop', '--time', stop_seconds.to_s, id, cleanup: true, seconds: stop_seconds + 5)\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"sqlserver\/manual-count-100m\/model.rb\",\n      \"old\": \"    receipts = probe.fetch('commits', [])\\n    conditions == CONDITIONS && samples.size == 18 &&\\n\",\n      \"new\": \"    receipts = probe.fetch('commits', [])\\n    smoke = probe['preload_monitor_smoke']\\n    smoke.is_a?(Hash) && smoke['status'] == 'passed' && smoke['accepted'] == true && smoke['errors'] == [] &&\\n      %w[before_load open_session_release_verified session_disposed_release_verified admin_disposed_release_verified].all? { |key| smoke[key] == true } &&\\n      conditions == CONDITIONS && samples.size == 18 &&\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"sqlserver\/manual-count-100m\/verify_offline.rb\",\n      \"old\": \"    'secondary_gate' => { 'secondary_rosetta_verified' => true },\\n\",\n      \"new\": \"    'secondary_gate' => { 'secondary_rosetta_verified' => true },\\n    'preload_monitor_smoke' => { 'status' => 'passed', 'accepted' => true, 'errors' => [], 'before_load' => true,\\n      'open_session_release_verified' => true, 'session_disposed_release_verified' => true, 'admin_disposed_release_verified' => true },\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"sqlserver\/manual-count-100m\/verify_offline.rb\",\n      \"old\": \"   :a_not_readable, :a_redo, :a_not_rosetta, :a_backup_failed, :changed_composite].each do |failure|\\n\",\n      \"new\": \"   :a_not_readable, :a_redo, :a_not_rosetta, :a_backup_failed, :changed_composite,\\n   :missing_smoke, :failed_smoke, :smoke_not_accepted, :smoke_error, :smoke_after_load,\\n   :smoke_open_not_idle, :smoke_session_survived, :smoke_admin_survived].each do |failure|\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"sqlserver\/manual-count-100m\/verify_offline.rb\",\n      \"old\": \"    case failure\\n    when :missing_sample then bad['samples'].pop\\n\",\n      \"new\": \"    case failure\\n    when :missing_smoke then bad.delete('preload_monitor_smoke')\\n    when :failed_smoke then bad['preload_monitor_smoke']['status'] = 'failed'\\n    when :smoke_not_accepted then bad['preload_monitor_smoke']['accepted'] = false\\n    when :smoke_error then bad['preload_monitor_smoke']['errors'] = ['monitor SQL failed']\\n    when :smoke_after_load then bad['preload_monitor_smoke']['before_load'] = false\\n    when :smoke_open_not_idle then bad['preload_monitor_smoke']['open_session_release_verified'] = false\\n    when :smoke_session_survived then bad['preload_monitor_smoke']['session_disposed_release_verified'] = false\\n    when :smoke_admin_survived then bad['preload_monitor_smoke']['admin_disposed_release_verified'] = false\\n    when :missing_sample then bad['samples'].pop\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"sqlserver\/manual-count-100m\/README.md\",\n      \"old\": \"Author runs only stdlib offline verification.\",\n      \"new\": \"Repair authors only read and propose exact replacements. The owner applies them after archiving the failed run and completing guarded cleanup of its owned data, then reruns the existing offline suite and fresh all; compilation and actual SQL execution remain owner-only.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"sqlserver\/manual-count-100m\/README.md\",\n      \"old\": \"Exactly 100,000,000 rows, 100 stored columns, 404 logical bytes before engine overhead. BIGINT precedes all offset\/multiplication; `c001` varied, `c002` 80% zero, `c003` high-cardinality, `c004..99` constant. One 1000 × 100k committed load, no second INSERT copy or full-target validation COUNT. Every commit receipt must match its exact contiguous ID boundaries and post-COMMIT transaction count zero.\\n\",\n      \"new\": \"Exactly 100,000,000 rows, 100 stored columns, 404 logical bytes before engine overhead. BIGINT precedes all offset\/multiplication; `c001` varied, `c002` 80% zero, `c003` high-cardinality, `c004..99` constant. One 1000 × 100k committed load, no second INSERT copy or full-target validation COUNT. Every commit receipt must match its exact contiguous ID boundaries and post-COMMIT transaction count zero.\\n\\nThe new canonical fixture adds `ORDER BY id OPTION (MAXDOP 1)` only to the INSERT SELECT, requesting PK-ordered loading while preserving every value formula and receipt boundary. Reduced split\/space overhead is an unmeasured improvement hypothesis until the fresh owner run. COUNT SQL\/hints, optimizer settings, cold protocol, index\/data geometry and count-case resource limits stay fixed; no post-load repair\/rebuild is added. Record and inspect the resulting actual planned-index pages and estimated plans as before.\\n\\nFailed owner run `20261108T213706Z-b0798be83c64c6dc5992bed4adae8ed5` completed all 1000 commits \/ 100M rows in approximately 945.88 seconds, then failed with `Incorrect syntax near 'WHEREs'.` in ObserveSql; release encountered the same SQL defect. It produced zero successful measured COUNTs. The raw run exited1; `docker stop --time 20` ended the primary at137, cleanup failed and the owned stage was retained. These remain failure evidence. The first fixture's PK page metadata reported `used_bytes=65,222,975,488` and `reserved_bytes=65,231,323,136`; preflight host free was 164,172,894,208 bytes. Two-node AG restore plus indexes\/logs\/tempdb\/backups has a narrow capacity margin. Ordered loading does not establish capacity sufficiency; all existing gates and actual resulting page\/plan checks remain mandatory.\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"sqlserver\/manual-count-100m\/README.md\",\n      \"old\": \"engine internals, hints\/MAXDOP, COUNT(1),\",\n      \"new\": \"engine internals, COUNT hints\/MAXDOP changes, COUNT(1),\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"sqlserver\/manual-count-100m\/README.md\",\n      \"old\": \"Before each cell: exact frozen inventory\/guard\/role SQL,\",\n      \"new\": \"After CREATE TABLE and the actual 100-column geometry\/settings checks, before the first fixture INSERT, run the actual preload monitor smoke on the new empty fixture. Two dedicated unpooled connections obtain independent Guard identities. The admin executes the same ObserveSql used by monitoring; the observed live connection GUID and Idle(false) must match, and Guard rechecks immutable identity. Release independently proves the open session idle. Both smoke connections are then disposed and independently verified absent through Release\/Idle(true) before load begins. Guard uses only the manual prefix; this smoke executes no Target COUNT and adds no condition\/sample to the eighteen slots. Persist status, identities, SQL, observation, errors and release flags in `preload-monitor-smoke.json` and `probe.preload_monitor_smoke`, with the Release histories under `cleanup\/`. Any smoke or connection-release failure aborts before insertion and prevents acceptance. The offline suite checks acceptance bookkeeping; actual SQL regression coverage occurs only in the owner's fresh all execution.\\n\\nBefore each cell: exact frozen inventory\/guard\/role SQL,\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"sqlserver\/manual-count-100m\/README.md\",\n      \"old\": \"Six-hour root deadline plus independent cleanup120 seconds;\",\n      \"new\": \"Six-hour root deadline plus independent cleanup240 seconds;\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"sqlserver\/manual-count-100m\/README.md\",\n      \"old\": \"Each started SQL server must exit0, not OOM\/137; stop errors preserved.\",\n      \"new\": \"Each SQL server gets60 seconds for orderly shutdown with a bounded65-second stop CLI; the client retains its20\/25-second stop\/CLI bounds. Each started SQL server must exit0; forced\/nonzero\/OOM exits and stop errors remain cleanup failures and preserve the stage.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"sqlserver\/manual-count-100m\/README.md\",\n      \"old\": \"Author offline pass is not that acceptance.\",\n      \"new\": \"Owner offline pass is not that acceptance.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"rationale\": {\n    \"measuredFailure\": {\n      \"run\": \"20261108T213706Z-b0798be83c64c6dc5992bed4adae8ed5\",\n      \"completedCommits\": 1000,\n      \"committedRows\": 100000000,\n      \"ownerReportedLoadSeconds\": 945.88,\n      \"successfulMeasuredCounts\": 0,\n      \"probeError\": \"Incorrect syntax near 'WHEREs'.\",\n      \"rawRunExitStatus\": 1,\n      \"clientExitStatus\": 1,\n      \"primaryTerminalExitStatus\": 137,\n      \"cleanup\": \"failed_or_unknown_preserved_evidence\",\n      \"ownedStageRetained\": true,\n      \"pkUsedBytes\": 65222975488,\n      \"pkReservedBytes\": 65231323136,\n      \"preflightFreeBytes\": 164172894208,\n      \"classification\": \"Failed benchmark and failed cleanup; successful insertion alone is not benchmark success.\"\n    },\n    \"sqlBoundaryAudit\": [\n      \"The first ObserveSql raw string ends at WHERE without a trailing newline. An explicit space before Match fixes the concrete WHEREs token concatenation.\",\n      \"The other four Match joins already end their preceding ordinary strings with a space. Each Match is followed by a semicolon\/newline before the next statement; StateSql therefore has a valid statement boundary.\",\n      \"Fixture.InsertSql joins the numeric offset immediately after CAST( and follows it with a leading-space AS BIGINT fragment. That punctuation boundary is valid and requires no whitespace repair.\",\n      \"No additional concrete concatenation defect was identified in the inspected Program.cs, Fixture.cs and State.cs SQL construction.\"\n    ],\n    \"smoke\": [\n      \"Runs after actual empty-table geometry\/settings validation and before starting the two-hour insertion budget.\",\n      \"Exercises actual Guard, immutable identity verification, ObserveSql and Idle(false), followed by independently connected Release checks for the live session and both disposed smoke sessions.\",\n      \"Attempts disposal\/release of both smoke connections even after a smoke failure, persists primary and cleanup errors, and propagates failure before insertion.\",\n      \"Uses no Target COUNT, sample, new condition, context tag or COUNT transaction wrapper. Acceptance additionally requires the persisted successful smoke and all release flags.\"\n    ],\n    \"shutdown\": [\n      \"Only SQL-server stop grace changes to60 seconds, with a65-second CLI bound; client stop bounds remain20\/25 seconds.\",\n      \"Independent overall cleanup budget becomes240 seconds. Ownership, pinned IDs, terminal-state checks, failure preservation, guest-side guarded unlink and stage-preservation conditions remain intact.\",\n      \"No capacity-reclamation wait, cache purge, restart or threshold relaxation is added. The original within1GiB capacity requirement remains.\"\n    ],\n    \"orderedLoader\": [\n      \"Only the fixture INSERT SELECT receives ORDER BY id OPTION (MAXDOP 1). Rows, stored columns, value formulas, batch boundaries and1000 receipts remain identical.\",\n      \"Lower split\/space overhead is predicted and unmeasured. The failed fixture's observed pages do not establish the new fixture's size or AG capacity sufficiency.\",\n      \"COUNT SQL\/hints, plans' observation procedure, cold protocol, six cells\/eighteen slots, count20min\/load2h\/global6h, host70\/index24\/floor12GiB, both nodes'2048MB SQL caps, Rosetta proofs and guarded cleanup remain unchanged.\"\n    ],\n    \"authorVerification\": \"No source was edited and no test, Docker, SQL or measurement execution was performed. Replacement uniqueness and compilation have not been executed as author checks. The supplied offline receipt binds the pre-repair owner18 inputs only.\"\n  },\n  \"offlineChecksRequired\": [\n    {\n      \"ownerAction\": \"After archiving the failed run and completing ownership-guarded cleanup of its retained data, verify the supplied pre-repair source hashes and require every old string to occur exactly once in its designated file before applying the replacements.\",\n      \"executionStatus\": \"not_run_by_author\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ownerAction\": \"Run the existing offline suite in the foreground from sqlserver\/manual-count-100m.\",\n      \"command\": \"mise exec -- ruby verify_offline.rb\",\n      \"requiredEvidence\": \"Terminal exit_status0 and complete stdout\/stderr log paths; retain the updated acceptance-negative cases. An incomplete log is not a passing check.\",\n      \"executionStatus\": \"not_run_by_author\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"ownerExecutionRequired\": [\n    {\n      \"command\": \"mise exec -- ruby lab.rb all\",\n      \"requirements\": \"Fresh owned execution after existing prerequisite gates; owner-only locked restore\/compilation and actual DB execution. Run in the foreground through terminal exit and retain complete CLI logs, exit statuses and source fingerprints.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirements\": \"Verify successful empty-fixture smoke and independent disposal\/release evidence before load; exactly1000 valid commit receipts and18 accepted COUNT results across the unchanged six cells; actual resulting pages\/plans, both-node Rosetta\/memory proofs and AG role\/restore evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirements\": \"Judge completion, precision, service budget and cleanup separately. Confirm both started SQL servers exit0, resource inventories and guarded guest unlink succeed, and capacity returns within1GiB. Preserve failed\/unknown outcomes and owned stages according to the existing rules.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirements\": \"Owner audits evidence meanings, final source and cleanup, followed by the existing two separate fresh GPT-6.1 Sol review roles.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"unresolvedIssues\": [\n    \"The proposal is uncompiled and unexecuted. Actual monitor SQL, disposal\/release smoke, ordered loading and orderly shutdown require the owner's fresh all run.\",\n    \"Ordered loading has no measured space or speed improvement yet; two-node AG capacity remains uncertain and must pass unchanged capacity gates.\",\n    \"A60-second server shutdown grace is unverified on this workload. Forced\/nonzero\/OOM shutdown must still fail cleanup.\",\n    \"During bounded JSON reading, the system python3 launcher unexpectedly emitted xcodebuild temporary-cache\/FSEvents diagnostics. The first heredoc read attempt was refused by the read-only filesystem; the subsequent JSON summary command exited0 with those diagnostics. Neither operation is verification evidence or a compiler\/build success.\"\n  ],\n  \"inputBindings\": {\n    \"sourceHashes\": {\n      \"sqlserver\/manual-count-100m\/lab.rb\": \"cf29973c3f852a7b7677bf68a642ee6dc33f1068302a49f84f242b236c1c3141\",\n      \"sqlserver\/manual-count-100m\/model.rb\": \"02255dbaee1ef53fd613e0b39ed55c61b0b9008182a9763cdd20737abaad41cd\",\n      \"sqlserver\/manual-count-100m\/verify_offline.rb\": \"fd56e75848018fb98d3b17322b65789429f0bfda63dc1b8ae939ea2278f27bfc\",\n      \"sqlserver\/manual-count-100m\/mise.toml\": \"44e7bbb5d9d1185e0e0848cfdfd782824836ee9feec2a9d1b0a99ba571e9acf4\",\n      \"sqlserver\/manual-count-100m\/compose.yaml\": \"5bf7fa606a0b7cffc9373d835f1df3232728bcca12285c5d26b614b00bef1080\",\n      \"sqlserver\/manual-count-100m\/Dockerfile\": \"4aea959a36994b64141267f612714177fbe0a07cacfbd2d5535741ab59815f04\",\n      \"sqlserver\/manual-count-100m\/.dockerignore\": \"0a1e42540e627caa3100565f190e6da9a82135cf5fc71b0a06f8a105d